+1 — same failure on macOS with gbrain v0.22.8 + gstack v1.26.4.0. Adding a correction: the suggested one-line rename is incomplete.

## Environment

- gstack 1.26.4.0
- gbrain 0.22.8 (also reproduced on a v0.27.0 checkout before reverting)
- macOS (Darwin 25.4.0), bun runtime

## The simple `put_page` -> `put` rename silently drops metadata

`gbrain put` only accepts `slug` (positional) + content (stdin). The `--title`, `--type`, and `--tags` flags are silently consumed:

```
$ echo "test body" | gbrain put gstack-test-flags --type test --tags foo,bar
$ gbrain get gstack-test-flags
---
type: concept
title: Gstack Test Flags
---
test body
```

Type came back as auto-derived `concept`, tags are empty. So a literal `put_page` -> `put` swap makes calls succeed but loses all the metadata gstack built (`repo:<slug>`, `agent:<name>`, content type, etc.).

Looking at gbrain/src/core/operations.ts:367:

```ts
cliHints: { name: 'put', positional: ['slug'], stdin: 'content' }
```

The `put_page` operation only takes `slug` and `content` over the CLI surface. Title/type/tags have to come from YAML frontmatter inside the body. (The `put_page` name itself is the operation/MCP name — it was, as far as I can tell, never a CLI subcommand. `cliHints.name` does the rename to `put`.)

## Working patch

Rewrote `gbrainPutPage()` at `bin/gstack-memory-ingest.ts:762` to inject metadata into the body's frontmatter (merging with existing frontmatter when present, since transcript pages already have an `agent:`/`session_id:` head):

```ts
function gbrainPutPage(page: PageRecord): { ok: boolean; error?: string } {
  if (!gbrainAvailable()) {
    return { ok: false, error: "gbrain CLI not in PATH" };
  }
  try {
    const yamlEscape = (s: string) => JSON.stringify(s);
    const yamlList = (xs: string[]) => \`[\${xs.map(yamlEscape).join(", ")}]\`;
    const metaLines = [
      \`title: \${yamlEscape(page.title)}\`,
      \`type: \${page.type}\`,
      \`tags: \${yamlList(page.tags)}\`,
    ];
    let body: string;
    if (page.body.startsWith("---\n")) {
      const closeIdx = page.body.indexOf("\n---", 4);
      if (closeIdx > 0) {
        const existingHead = page.body.slice(4, closeIdx);
        const rest = page.body.slice(closeIdx + 4);
        body = ["---", ...metaLines, existingHead.trimEnd(), "---", rest.replace(/^\n/, "")].join("\n");
      } else {
        body = ["---", ...metaLines, "---", "", page.body].join("\n");
      }
    } else {
      body = ["---", ...metaLines, "---", "", page.body].join("\n");
    }
    execFileSync("gbrain", ["put", page.slug], {
      input: body,
      encoding: "utf-8",
      timeout: 30000,
      stdio: ["pipe", "pipe", "pipe"],
    });
    return { ok: true };
  } catch (err) {
    return { ok: false, error: err instanceof Error ? err.message : String(err) };
  }
}
```

After patch: 15 curated artifacts (CEO plans, design docs, learnings, timelines) ingested cleanly with correct types/tags preserved. `gbrain list -n` shows the right titles and types; semantic search ranks them as expected. 0 failed in a `--bulk --sources eureka,learning,timeline,ceo-plan,design-doc,retro,builder-profile-entry` run.

