### Proposed fix (two-layer defense)

I've drafted the fix based on the suggested guard in this issue. Two changes needed:

**1. `decideResume()` in `gstack-gbrain-sync.ts`** — before returning `{ kind: "resume" }`, validate that `cp.dir` resolves to a path under `/.staging-ingest-`:

```typescript
const stagingPrefix = resolve(GSTACK_HOME, ".staging-ingest-");
const resolved = (() => { try { return realpathSync(stagingDir); } catch { return null; } })();
if (resolved === null || !resolved.startsWith(stagingPrefix)) {
  console.error(`[sync:memory] checkpoint.dir "${stagingDir}" is not a gstack staging dir; skipping resume.`);
  return { kind: "stale-staging-missing", stagingDir };
}
```

**2. `cleanupStagingDir()` in `gstack-memory-ingest.ts`** — second line of defense at the delete site:

```typescript
function cleanupStagingDir(dir: string): void {
  const stagingPrefix = resolve(GSTACK_HOME, ".staging-ingest-");
  let canonDir: string;
  try { canonDir = realpathSync(dir); } catch { return; }
  if (!canonDir.startsWith(stagingPrefix)) {
    console.error(`[gbrain] BUG: cleanupStagingDir called on non-staging path "${dir}"; refusing.`);
    return;
  }
  try { rmSync(dir, { recursive: true, force: true }); } catch { /* best-effort */ }
}
```

